  "summary_en": "UK Competition and Markets Authority update report on AI foundation models. It reviews market developments since September 2023, confirms competition and consumer-protection principles, identifies three key risks to fair, open and effective competition (control of inputs, incumbent distortion, partnerships), and sets next steps. Embodied AI is not addressed.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Confirms CMA principles to guide foundation model markets: access, diversity, choice, flexibility, fair dealing, transparency",
   "Identifies three risks: restricted access to critical inputs, incumbents distorting choice, partnerships entrenching market power",
   "Notes the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Bill would give CMA direct consumer enforcement powers with fines up to 10% of turnover",
   "Observes growing presence of GAMMA firms across the foundation model value chain",
   "Plans a paper on AI accelerator chips and further update in autumn 2024"
